WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.719
♪ [music] ♪

00:00:06.256 --> 00:00:09.400
[Stephanie] Give me one minute,
and I'll show you how Cloud Spanner

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.084
can help you create real-time,
mission-critical applications at scale.

00:00:13.084 --> 00:00:15.325
Spanner is a fully managed
relational database

00:00:15.325 --> 00:00:17.563
with unlimited scale, strong consistency,

00:00:17.563 --> 00:00:20.858
and up to 99.999% availability.

00:00:20.858 --> 00:00:23.322
Most databases today
require making a trade-off

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:25.442
between scale and consistency.

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:27.924
With Spanner, you get the best
of relational semantics

00:00:27.924 --> 00:00:29.683
and non-relational scale.

00:00:29.683 --> 00:00:32.370
It uses TrueTime, which provides
a global notion of time,

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:34.229
allowing it to scale horizontally,

00:00:34.229 --> 00:00:36.895
while still delivering
strong external consistency

00:00:36.895 --> 00:00:39.399
across rows, regions, and continents.

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:43.190
You can serve data with low latency
and deliver a unified experience.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.862
Your IT admins, DBAs, and developers
can spin up globally replicated databases

00:00:47.862 --> 00:00:51.200
in just a handful of clicks,
using the Google Cloud Console.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.908
Just enter a name, instance ID,
location, and number of nodes,

00:00:54.908 --> 00:00:58.096
or they can create it using
the gcloud command-line interface.

00:00:58.096 --> 00:01:00.601
From there, create a database
and define a schema.

00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:02.016
It's that simple!

00:01:02.016 --> 00:01:04.495
You can expect everything
from a relational database,

00:01:04.495 --> 00:01:07.243
schemas, SQL queries,
and ACID transactions.

00:01:07.243 --> 00:01:12.101
You get a 99.999% availability SLA
through Spanner's automatic replicas,

00:01:12.101 --> 00:01:14.940
no planned downtime,
and online schema changes.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.347
With manage backup and restore,
don't worry about data corruption.

00:01:18.347 --> 00:01:21.083
Based on resource speed
requirements and data retention,

00:01:21.083 --> 00:01:23.658
you can also import and export data.

00:01:23.658 --> 00:01:26.360
And data is encrypted
at rest and in transit,

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.312
providing you full security.

00:01:28.312 --> 00:01:31.885
Spanner's a perfect choice for high-scale
online transaction processing

00:01:31.885 --> 00:01:34.005
and real-time decision-making workloads

00:01:34.005 --> 00:01:38.729
in industries like retail, gaming,
healthcare, financial services, and more.

00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:41.914
So, next time you want to deliver
mission-critical apps at scale

00:01:41.914 --> 00:01:44.059
and a unified experience
with low maintenance,

00:01:44.059 --> 00:01:45.911
take a minute to look at Cloud Spanner.

00:01:45.911 --> 00:01:49.028
To learn more, check out
cloud.google.com/spanner

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:53.881
♪ [music] ♪

